= Epistemics =

BITwiki makes the basis and limits of knowledge visible rather than treating all statements as equivalent.

== Core primitives ==
* '''Source''' — where information originates.
* '''Evidence''' — what supports a claim.
* '''Provenance''' — how content entered and changed within the knowledge system.
* '''Epistemic status''' — the kind or maturity of a knowledge claim.
* '''Confidence''' — how strongly the available evidence supports the current representation.
* '''Uncertainty''' — what remains unknown, estimated, conditional, or disputed.
* '''Verification''' — when and how information was checked.

== Granularity ==
Epistemic information may apply to a page, section, claim, or citation. It should use citations and semantic metadata where appropriate rather than becoming a sprawling category hierarchy.

== Principle ==
Explicit perspective is compatible with rigor when sources, evidence, assumptions, and uncertainty remain inspectable.

